      "provenance": {
        "notes": "Genus-level entry for the hybrids (the African violet row 19 stays separate). Watering conflict: Clemson (S. saxorum) says keep evenly damp, NC State and RHS say let the compost dry slightly between waterings; the two-source reading is kept. The Clemson page is for S. saxorum and its figures (60 to 75 F, 8 by 12 in) are for that species; the RHS size is for the hybrid 'Cariad' (10 to 50 cm), upper values. Habit rosette follows NC State 'most commonly a basal rosette'. Humidity is high per NC State but no number."
      },
